## Request

Make the existing App Server selector and dispatcher one accountable operation for eligible Tool
Shed work. Prefer the smallest implementation: either select and dispatch in one command or issue a
short-lived dispatch lease that the dispatcher must consume. Preserve the current supported roles,
model/reasoning policy, qualification, authentication, safety checks, and bounded CAMP runner.

Use one correlation ID from opportunity through attempt and one controlled terminal result. Treat
completed, default-mode pre-mutation GUI fallback, and post-mutation reconciliation-required as the
only terminal branches. An incomplete process remains explicit pending debt and cannot be mistaken
for a normal GUI continuation. Do not add closure gating, cross-platform release qualification, or
production delivery beyond the minimal M1 interface needed for the later campaign.

